# harness/field/scenarios/load.expect: where load.sh's rust leg is known to differ from MIT's, by check name (the INFO
# observations of checks.tsv). The comparison of the two legs grades a listed check KNOWN; anything else that differs
# is a finding. Each line names the hand record that shows the difference and what would remove it.
# check	known difference (rust leg vs MIT)	record	removed by
LD.rss.base	daemon RSS before the load: krb5kdc about 27 MiB where MIT's is about 5 MiB	upgrade.expect obs.rss.start; none: the LD cells' first record	P16 (investigation)
LD.rss.first	as LD.rss.base, the series' first sample	as LD.rss.base	P16 (investigation)
LD.rss.last	RSS at the end of the load; the rust leg's is bounded by LD.rss.cap, MIT's is recorded only	as LD.rss.base	P16 (investigation)
LD.rss.max	as LD.rss.last, the series' largest sample	as LD.rss.base	P16 (investigation)
LD.rss.cap	graded on the rust leg only (last <= first * 1.5 + 33 MiB); an INFO row on MIT's	none: the LD cells' first record	a bound on MIT's too, if MIT's RSS is wanted graded
LD.rss.slope	graded on the rust leg only (<= 0.05 MiB/s from 300 s, when that window spans 300 s); an INFO row on MIT's	none: the LD cells' first record	a bound on MIT's too, if MIT's RSS is wanted graded
LD.load.throughput	loadgen's kinit + TGS per second differs between the KDCs (a measurement, not a result)	none: the LD cells' first record	nothing: the number is recorded for the trend
